Impact Analysis for Public APIs
What Remains Covered

WAF & DDoS

TLS termination

Route-based rate limiting

JWT validation

Global caching

Reverse proxy routing

Path rewrite handled via Istio VirtualService

What Is Lost Without APIM

Native subscription key management

Built-in developer portal

API product bundling

Version governance tooling

Per-consumer quotas

Centralized Azure API governance

Benefits of Removing APIM

Reduced latency (one hop removed)

Reduced Azure cost

Simpler architecture

Fewer moving parts

Security remains enforced at Cloudflare edge

Istio already handles routing and rewrite logic

Risks

Public API governance shifts away from Azure

Consumer onboarding must be handled externally

Subscription-based access control must move to:

Application layer

Cloudflare Workers

Loss of built-in developer portal

Executive Summary

For security, routing, caching, and path management, Cloudflare + Istio can replace APIM capabilities.

For public API governance, subscription management, developer portal, and structured API lifecycle control, APIM still provides additional value.

Removing APIM is technically feasible without breaking existing URLs (Istio VirtualService already manages the /md/ prefix rewrite). The final decision depends on whether the priority is:

Edge security and architectural simplification
or

Structured public API governance and consumer management.
